1
00:00:00,010 --> 00:00:01,829
Welcome to ResGrid Academy.

2
00:00:01,980 --> 00:00:06,220
In this lesson, we will understand
AI availability and human review.

3
00:00:06,400 --> 00:00:11,030
AI product descriptions and code can
move ahead of deployment availability.

4
00:00:11,210 --> 00:00:14,809
So training must distinguish
released tools from planned ones.

5
00:00:14,980 --> 00:00:18,709
We will explain the features,
the setup decisions, and a

6
00:00:18,709 --> 00:00:20,829
practical way to check the result.

7
00:00:21,619 --> 00:00:25,689
An administrator asks Admin Assist
why a member was not paged and

8
00:00:25,689 --> 00:00:27,709
reviews the evidence it links to.

9
00:00:27,900 --> 00:00:31,779
Get explanations and drafts
for people to review alongside

10
00:00:31,779 --> 00:00:33,409
the tools you already use.

11
00:00:33,570 --> 00:00:37,549
The examples in this series use a
fictional department and are teaching

12
00:00:37,549 --> 00:00:39,989
scenarios, not default settings.

13
00:00:40,809 --> 00:00:41,979
Enhanced AI.

14
00:00:42,480 --> 00:00:45,619
AI assistants beyond the
free Admin Assist allowance.

15
00:00:45,829 --> 00:00:47,310
Nothing to set up yet.

16
00:00:47,419 --> 00:00:50,229
Your free Admin Assist
allowance works without it.

17
00:00:50,399 --> 00:00:53,199
This feature is marked
Planned in the source catalog.

18
00:00:53,389 --> 00:00:57,949
Verify release availability before
recording a configuration walkthrough.

19
00:00:58,739 --> 00:01:02,499
The checkout contains gated AI
dispatch settings for enrichment

20
00:01:02,509 --> 00:01:07,819
fields, confidence, sender scope,
token limits, and activity.

21
00:01:08,010 --> 00:01:12,440
Confirm host enablement and department
rollout before reviewing the settings.

22
00:01:12,680 --> 00:01:15,529
Saving settings alone
does not start enrichment.

23
00:01:15,709 --> 00:01:19,659
Check the running state,
activity outcomes, and usage.

24
00:01:19,860 --> 00:01:23,789
This source present feature is
unverified on the target deployment.

25
00:01:23,939 --> 00:01:26,950
Confirm availability in
the demo department before

26
00:01:26,950 --> 00:01:28,609
recording the live workflow.

27
00:01:29,430 --> 00:01:32,349
For the training scenario,
work in this order.

28
00:01:32,549 --> 00:01:36,510
Step one, use deterministic
setup wizard and setup report

29
00:01:36,510 --> 00:01:38,309
for configuration guidance.

30
00:01:38,570 --> 00:01:43,129
Step two, check whether admin AI is
enabled for the target department.

31
00:01:43,329 --> 00:01:46,599
Step three, check release
and rollout before teaching

32
00:01:46,599 --> 00:01:48,769
enhanced AI summaries or drafts.

33
00:01:49,750 --> 00:01:51,389
Now verify the result.

34
00:01:51,589 --> 00:01:55,760
Record the target deployment version
and observed feature availability.

35
00:01:55,949 --> 00:02:00,739
Human reviewers remain responsible for
any generated explanation or draft.

36
00:02:00,889 --> 00:02:04,619
A common problem to watch for,
the catalog in this checkout

37
00:02:04,659 --> 00:02:06,639
marks Enhanced AI as planned.

38
00:02:06,829 --> 00:02:08,840
This lesson explains its scope.

39
00:02:09,020 --> 00:02:12,029
It does not demonstrate
a released configuration.

40
00:02:12,830 --> 00:02:14,679
Your practice task is simple.

41
00:02:14,849 --> 00:02:18,890
Ask a configuration question
through an available tool, inspect

42
00:02:18,890 --> 00:02:23,250
its evidence, and identify any
unknowns before making a change.

43
00:02:23,429 --> 00:02:27,949
Record the result, who owns the follow
up, and when it should be reviewed.

44
00:02:28,080 --> 00:02:32,060
Use the linked feature scripts for
the detailed screen recording plan.
